00:09:30.958 --> 00:09:33.750
He is second in the NFL
with nine total touchdowns.

00:09:33.750 --> 00:09:35.958
He's averaging
over five yards a carry.

00:09:35.958 --> 00:09:38.750
And the Chargers
are quietly 4-2.

00:09:38.750 --> 00:09:40.708
- Yes.
- And the offense is clicking.

00:09:40.708 --> 00:09:43.458
And I think Melvin Gordon
is the piece that's making them

00:09:43.458 --> 00:09:45.000
one of the elite teams
in the NFL.

00:09:45.000 --> 00:09:48.125
- No. 3, yes.
Captain America, J.J. Watt.

00:09:48.125 --> 00:09:51.333
He's back. He's one of the best
defensive players in football.

00:09:51.333 --> 00:09:54.125
He's tied for the league
lead in sacks with seven sacks.

00:09:54.125 --> 00:09:56.375
He's tied for the league lead
in forced fumbles

00:09:56.375 --> 00:09:57.750
with four forced fumbles.

00:09:57.750 --> 00:10:00.333
He is awesome.
He's extremely disruptive.

00:10:00.333 --> 00:10:02.042
He'd be another guy that
we gotta show some love

00:10:02.042 --> 00:10:03.792
and throw him in the mix here.
- Look at the stats.

00:10:03.792 --> 00:10:05.875
The Texans defense
is shuttin' people down.

00:10:05.875 --> 00:10:07.667
- It is.
- Look at the stats for my man

00:10:07.667 --> 00:10:10.042
Khalil Mack.
- Oh, Mack is Khalil-ing it!

00:10:10.042 --> 00:10:11.667
- Oh, man.
- You like that?

00:10:11.667 --> 00:10:13.292
- So, he's tied with—
eh, it was OK.
- OK.

00:10:13.292 --> 00:10:15.875
He's tied with J.J.
for four forced fumbles.

00:10:15.875 --> 00:10:18.042
And, really, just look
at the Raiders defense.

00:10:18.042 --> 00:10:19.667
- Yes.
- And then look at what he did

00:10:19.667 --> 00:10:21.042
for the Bears defense.

00:10:21.042 --> 00:10:23.417
- It changed the mantra
of their team.

00:10:23.417 --> 00:10:25.417
- No. 1?
- No. 1 is Todd Gurley.

00:10:25.417 --> 00:10:27.667
The best running back
in the NFL right now.

00:10:27.667 --> 00:10:30.125
I mean, Gurley is leading
the league in yards per game

00:10:30.125 --> 00:10:31.792
as far as rushing yards.

00:10:31.792 --> 00:10:34.292
He's leading the league
with 11 touchdowns right now.

00:10:34.292 --> 00:10:35.917
He's awesome
between the tackles

00:10:35.917 --> 00:10:37.750
like we saw against
the Broncos last week.

00:10:37.750 --> 00:10:39.625
If there's nothin' there
between the tackles

00:10:39.625 --> 00:10:42.167
he can bounce it outside
and run by everybody.

00:10:42.167 --> 00:10:43.833
He's great in the pass game

00:10:43.833 --> 00:10:48.167
and he is really the guy
that makes that offense work.

00:10:48.167 --> 00:10:50.167
Todd Gurley is amazing.
He really is.

00:10:50.167 --> 00:10:52.333
I like this list. This is fun.
- All right.

00:10:52.333 --> 00:10:55.958
So, these are guys that
probably won't win the MVP

00:10:55.958 --> 00:10:57.417
cuz they're not quarterbacks.

00:10:57.417 --> 00:10:58.958
And there was a guy
on my favorite team

00:10:58.958 --> 00:11:00.958
the Philadelphia Eagles,
who had a performance

00:11:00.958 --> 00:11:02.667
that was MVP-worthy
in the Super Bowl.

00:11:02.667 --> 00:11:03.917
- Yeah.
- Terrell Owens.

00:11:03.917 --> 00:11:05.792
- T.O.
- But it's what happened

00:11:05.792 --> 00:11:08.583
a year or two later
that I'll never forget.

00:11:08.583 --> 00:11:12.208
- What did you say to Andy
to get kicked out of camp?

00:11:12.208 --> 00:11:15.208
♪♪

00:11:15.208 --> 00:11:18.208
- I was home from school,
and I was watchin' you.

00:11:18.208 --> 00:11:19.667
There was helicopters.

00:11:19.667 --> 00:11:21.583
Like, can you take me
to that day, please?

00:11:21.583 --> 00:11:23.833
- This was during training camp,
and this particular day

00:11:23.833 --> 00:11:25.750
it was the receivers' day
to sign autographs.

00:11:25.750 --> 00:11:28.750
Well, so, I had
a groin issue at the time

00:11:28.750 --> 00:11:30.875
so I just felt like,
"Let me use this time

00:11:30.875 --> 00:11:33.375
to go get myself healthier
in the training room."

00:11:33.375 --> 00:11:35.250
We had a bit of a disagreement.

00:11:35.250 --> 00:11:36.875
And it was, like,
right in the doorway

00:11:36.875 --> 00:11:38.250
of where, you know,
people were—

00:11:38.250 --> 00:11:39.958
- A lot of players
and coaches saw it.

00:11:39.958 --> 00:11:41.833
- Yeah, and I think some
other people just, you know

00:11:41.833 --> 00:11:43.458
listened to the conversation.
- Right, right.

00:11:43.458 --> 00:11:45.250
- So, you know, he felt like
I was showin' him up.

00:11:45.250 --> 00:11:47.208
And Coach said, "Go home."

00:11:47.208 --> 00:11:50.000
"In the meantime," he said,
"Keep yourself in shape while you're at it."

00:11:50.000 --> 00:11:52.708
I'm in the house
maybe 20, 25 minutes.

00:11:52.708 --> 00:11:55.458
I start hearin' helicopters
or whatever

00:11:55.458 --> 00:11:57.000
but I didn't think much of it.

00:11:57.000 --> 00:11:59.083
Somebody came
and knocked at the door.

00:11:59.083 --> 00:12:00.625
And I looked through the blinds.

00:12:00.625 --> 00:12:03.375
News trucks
were all out in my yard.

00:12:03.375 --> 00:12:05.917
The helicopters and everybody
was around my house.

00:12:05.917 --> 00:12:07.792
I just tried
to have fun with it.

00:12:07.792 --> 00:12:11.167
Saw my ab bench,
took it outside.

00:12:11.167 --> 00:12:13.542
I was, ya know,
entertaining the reporters

00:12:13.542 --> 00:12:15.750
and I was workin' out
at the same time.

00:12:15.750 --> 00:12:18.417
Little did anybody know,
I had an earpiece on.

00:12:18.417 --> 00:12:20.167
I called my publicist
at the time.

00:12:20.167 --> 00:12:24.417
She was listening to every question
that was being asked of me.

00:12:24.417 --> 00:12:26.417
And so she told me kind of
what to say, what not to say.

00:12:26.417 --> 00:12:28.667
And so I just basically said,
"No comment," or whatever.

00:12:28.667 --> 00:12:31.042
- Right.
- So, did you go back and you're like

00:12:31.042 --> 00:12:32.667
"Andy, I was keepin' myself in shape."

00:12:32.667 --> 00:12:34.292
- Well, yeah. I mean,
at some point

00:12:34.292 --> 00:12:35.042
he kinda figured that out.

00:12:37.792 --> 00:12:40.042
- T.O.'s the man. Ochocinco's the man.
- Yes.

00:12:40.042 --> 00:12:41.833
- And we sat with them
for a long time.

00:12:41.833 --> 00:12:43.792
They talked about
how hard it was

00:12:43.792 --> 00:12:45.958
for the public to know
who they really were—

00:12:45.958 --> 00:12:48.250
- Yeah.
- Cuz the media covered them a certain way.

00:12:48.250 --> 00:12:49.708
- Yeah.
- And I sit here now

00:12:49.708 --> 00:12:51.208
and I look at Odell Beckham Jr.

00:12:51.208 --> 00:12:53.333
And I'm hearin' quotes
from John Mara saying

00:12:53.333 --> 00:12:56.250
"I wish he'd create headlines
on the field instead of off."

00:12:56.250 --> 00:12:58.458
How can he create a headline
on the field—
- Yes!

00:12:58.458 --> 00:13:00.958
- When the quarterback can't
throw it more than five yards?

00:13:00.958 --> 00:13:02.833
- That is exactly right.
What can he do?

00:13:02.833 --> 00:13:04.625
And I'll bring this
to everybody's attention.

00:13:04.625 --> 00:13:08.333
I mean, we haven't heard
any reports about Giants players

00:13:08.333 --> 00:13:10.875
in the locker room
not liking Odell Beckham Jr.

00:13:10.875 --> 00:13:12.625
Those are the things
I listen to.

00:13:12.625 --> 00:13:14.208
There's no "anonymous" reports

00:13:14.208 --> 00:13:16.750
that locker room's divided
by Odell Beckham Jr.

00:13:16.750 --> 00:13:18.583
- Yes.
- We've talked to players.

00:13:18.583 --> 00:13:20.375
I've talked to people
with the Giants.

00:13:20.375 --> 00:13:22.250
- They love him.
- Odell is loved.

00:13:22.250 --> 00:13:24.208
- Would you rather a guy
be so passionate

00:13:24.208 --> 00:13:26.208
on the sideline
that he yells at himself

00:13:26.208 --> 00:13:30.417
or would you rather a guy
on the sideline sit like this?

00:13:30.417 --> 00:13:32.000
Simple question.
- Yeah.

00:13:32.000 --> 00:13:33.792
- And if you're at home
sittin' like that—

00:13:33.792 --> 00:13:35.750
Simms, do it.

00:13:35.750 --> 00:13:40.042
You may have contracted a very
troubling disease called Elitis.

00:13:40.042 --> 00:13:41.417
- Ooh, sounds serious.

00:13:41.417 --> 00:13:43.042
- It is.
- Yeah.

00:13:43.042 --> 00:13:46.500
- Do you blame the O-line for the
Giants' poor start?

00:13:46.500 --> 00:13:47.833
Do you believe quarterbacks
should be measured

00:13:47.833 --> 00:13:50.083
by completion
percentage?

00:13:50.083 --> 00:13:54.542
Have you ever been arrested
for defending Eli Manning’s honor?

00:13:54.542 --> 00:14:00.000
If you answered "yes" to any of these questions,
you may be suffering from a disorder known as–

00:14:00.000 --> 00:14:01.792
Elitis.

00:14:01.792 --> 00:14:04.333
This condition makes otherwise rational fans

00:14:04.333 --> 00:14:09.167
believe 37-year-old Eli Manning
is still the answer.

00:14:09.167 --> 00:14:11.417
Symptoms of Elitis
include yelling

00:14:11.417 --> 00:14:14.667
"2 rings” at co-workers,
and arguing that

00:14:14.667 --> 00:14:19.667
17 is actually the perfect amount
of points to score in a football game.

00:14:19.667 --> 00:14:23.667
Fortunately, there is a cure for Elitis.

00:14:23.667 --> 00:14:27.917
Unfortunately, that cure now plays for the Jets.

00:14:27.917 --> 00:14:31.875
So take your medicine, Giants fans.
You got what you wanted.

00:14:31.875 --> 00:14:34.333
At least Saquon is fun to watch.

00:14:34.333 --> 00:14:36.333
Too bad he can’t throw the ball.

00:14:48.417 --> 00:14:51.583
- All right, so thus far
on "Somebody &amp; Lefkoe"

00:14:51.583 --> 00:14:54.708
our pickers have done
pretty well: 3-3.

00:14:54.708 --> 00:14:56.583
Allie, Ira and Steve.

00:14:56.583 --> 00:14:58.458
But we're looking
for somebody special

00:14:58.458 --> 00:15:01.458
somebody whose picks won't be,
I don't know, falafel.

00:15:01.458 --> 00:15:04.417
Someone whose picks
you could kebab your head to.

00:15:04.417 --> 00:15:08.417
I'm looking for a gyro.
And that man is "The Dragon."

00:15:10.583 --> 00:15:12.708
So I'm tired of
gettin' bad information

00:15:12.708 --> 00:15:16.167
so I'm goin' to a guy
that only produces quality.

00:15:16.167 --> 00:15:20.583
Tony Dragonas,
aka "The Dragon."

00:15:20.583 --> 00:15:22.083
He breathes fire.

00:15:22.083 --> 00:15:24.708
We are at the corner
of 62nd and Madison

00:15:24.708 --> 00:15:27.208
and I have an incredible game
for you on Thursday night.

00:15:27.208 --> 00:15:29.833
Like, Super Bowl matchup.

00:15:29.833 --> 00:15:32.542
Denver-Arizona.
Can you feel the excitement?

00:15:32.542 --> 00:15:34.208
- I do. I do.
- Yeah.

00:15:34.208 --> 00:15:37.708
- Actually, I think Denver's
gonna beat the Cardinals.

00:15:37.708 --> 00:15:39.083
- You think so?
- Yeah.

00:15:39.083 --> 00:15:40.708
- Now, here's the deal.
Here's the line.

00:15:40.708 --> 00:15:44.208
Denver is favored by 2.5,
so they have to win by 2.5.

00:15:44.208 --> 00:15:45.833
Do you think they'll cover that?

00:15:45.833 --> 00:15:48.583
- Yes, because offense
of Arizona is not so strong.

00:15:48.583 --> 00:15:50.583
- It is not that strong.
- No, no.

00:15:50.583 --> 00:15:52.333
They have better offense.

00:15:52.333 --> 00:15:55.458
- We'll see if Tony can be my
"gyro" and get this game right.

00:15:55.458 --> 00:15:57.708
See what I did?
I combined "gyro" and "hero"?

00:15:57.708 --> 00:16:00.958
- [Laughing]
- It was good. Just laugh.

00:16:00.958 --> 00:16:02.583
So, Super Steve didn't make it.

00:16:02.583 --> 00:16:04.833
- Sorry, Scuba Steve.
See ya next time.

00:16:04.833 --> 00:16:09.125
Slimms the Oracle is back,
pickin' Thursday roadies!

00:16:09.125 --> 00:16:10.500
- The Dragon has entered.

00:16:10.500 --> 00:16:13.500
He's taking Denver minus-2.5
in Arizona.

00:16:13.500 --> 00:16:16.042
He doesn't think Arizona's
offense is gonna get it done.

00:16:16.042 --> 00:16:18.417
- Ooh!
I'm gonna train this Dragon.

00:16:18.417 --> 00:16:21.125
"How to Train Your Dragon,"
and I'm goin' with him!

00:16:21.125 --> 00:16:22.417
I'm ridin' The Dragon!

00:16:22.417 --> 00:16:25.042
- Wow!
- Yeehaw! I'm ridin' it.

00:16:25.042 --> 00:16:26.750
- Awesome.
- I like it.

00:16:26.750 --> 00:16:29.042
- I'm doubting that you learned
that from Bill Belichick.

00:16:29.042 --> 00:16:30.417
- No.
- But you've learned a lot

00:16:30.417 --> 00:16:32.167
from Bill Belichick.
- I have.

00:16:32.167 --> 00:16:34.792
- And we wish that other teams
would learn from Belichick, too.

00:16:34.792 --> 00:16:36.625
- Please!
- It's a little thing we call

00:16:36.625 --> 00:16:39.750
- [In unison] WWBD?
- What Would Belichick Do?

00:16:39.750 --> 00:16:42.000
And you've noticed some trends
from him this year

00:16:42.000 --> 00:16:44.292
that you think
he zigs when everybody zags.

00:16:44.292 --> 00:16:46.292
- Yes. You know
what he did this year?

00:16:46.292 --> 00:16:49.667
He drafted a between-the-tackles
running back in the first round.

00:16:49.667 --> 00:16:53.625
He drafted a tackle, offensive
tackle in the first round.

00:16:53.625 --> 00:16:56.708
I think he's goin',
"I don't think defenses
and defensive coaches

00:16:56.708 --> 00:16:58.417
are very good
at tackling anymore.

00:16:58.417 --> 00:17:00.208
They're so used
to the spread game.

00:17:00.208 --> 00:17:02.958
They're not used to taking on
pulling guards and fullbacks."

00:17:02.958 --> 00:17:04.917
And I think we're
slowly seeing New England

00:17:04.917 --> 00:17:07.458
get back into two backs,
one tight end.

00:17:07.458 --> 00:17:09.083
- Power running.
- Old-school football

00:17:09.083 --> 00:17:10.833
like we saw on Sunday night
against the Chiefs.

00:17:10.833 --> 00:17:12.458
- So you're saying
during the year

00:17:12.458 --> 00:17:14.458
we've had more 400-yard passers

00:17:14.458 --> 00:17:16.542
up to this point
than ever before.
- Yep.

00:17:16.542 --> 00:17:18.583
- Belichick's goin',
"We're gonna ground-and-pound."

00:17:18.583 --> 00:17:20.083
- I think
that's what we're seeing.

00:17:20.083 --> 00:17:21.958
- They're takin' on the Bears
this weekend.

00:17:21.958 --> 00:17:23.458
Maybe he keeps it running.

00:17:23.458 --> 00:17:25.208
But watch the Patriots
this year.

00:17:25.208 --> 00:17:28.083
If you notice things they do
that other teams don't do

00:17:28.083 --> 00:17:29.708
#WWBD?

00:17:29.708 --> 00:17:32.708
Be smarter. Follow the
greatest coach of all time.

00:17:32.708 --> 00:17:34.208
- Right.
- For Simms

00:17:34.208 --> 00:17:35.917
- Peace out, homies.
- I am the L-E-F-K-O-E.

00:17:35.917 --> 00:17:37.583
- Man.

00:17:37.583 --> 00:17:39.625
- And it's always been
a pleasure. Enjoy the games.

00:17:42.042 --> 00:17:46.167
- That's a lot of words you wrote.
- Ready, set, flip.

00:17:46.167 --> 00:17:50.542
- Who'd you say? Khaleesi's husband?
That's the same answer.

00:17:50.542 --> 00:17:51.833
- No it's not!
- Oooh!

00:17:51.833 --> 00:17:54.792
- Jon Snow is not Khaleesi's husband!
- Let's go!

00:17:54.792 --> 00:17:57.667
- Soon to be.
- She's soon to be!
462
00:17:57,667 --&gt; 00:00:00,000
- Let's go!
- Whoo!

